From b5f5d94e51c3525dbfd9727611059bd80028bcdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:42:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] tourism: the layer event last, the slice window reset
 before the pass, window 0 not -0 (B3 fix round)

verify-a minors 2 and 3. venuePass emits nothing; the daily (after the window reset), the tick (after a
fallback pass's attract step), refresh and init emit layerUpdated 'tourism' as their last statement, so a
listener that throws leaves the saved pass and the slice record complete. Before, the saved pass stayed last
month's while the records and raster in memory were new, and a save on dom 26-29 restored the old ones.
tourismWindow adds 0: the days before a city's first TOURISM_DAY gave -0, which a save stores as 0.
Bit-identical otherwise: no sim system listens to the 'tourism' layer event.

Tests: a listener that throws on the pass day (saves on days 56-59 continue field by field and by digest);
a save in the city's first month, loaded through the bundle codec and through a structured clone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KT9tXthEhyzExdUuGEecAJ
